# What does NOT go into the .vsix.
#
# The default is "everything git does not ignore", which for this extension was 66 files
# and 171 KB: the TypeScript sources, the whole test suite, the lint config, the mise task
# file. An installer would have received all of it.
#
# This is an exclusion list because that is the format vsce reads, but the rule it encodes
# is an allowlist — `scripts/check-package.ts` asserts that what comes out is exactly the
# runtime set, so adding a directory here is not enough to keep it out and forgetting to
# add one is not enough to let it in.

# ── the sources the build already turned into out/ ──────────────────────────
src/**
test/**
scripts/**

# Source maps point at `src/`, which is not shipped. A map whose sources are absent
# resolves to nothing and costs 78 KB saying so.
out/**/*.js.map

# ── build and lint configuration, which runs nowhere after packaging ────────
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.test.json
eslint.config.mjs
mise.toml
.gitignore
.vscodeignore
package-lock.json

# ── never ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/**
**/*.vsix
.local/**

# The Marketplace icon's source. `resources/icon.png` is what package.json names and what
# ships; the SVG it was rendered from stays in git for the next render and is dead weight
# in the package.
resources/icon.svg
